## Overview

This is a Spring Boot PetClinic variant where a single endpoint, `POST /api/owners` (plus `GET /api/owners/{id}`), derives a large set of owner-identity values. The identity fields are computed on-the-fly by getters on the `Owner` entity, delegating to small single-purpose helper classes in `model/` and `util/`. DTOs are generated by the OpenAPI generator from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (there are no hand-written `OwnerDto.java` files; they live under `target/generated-sources`).

Important discrepancy to note up front: the acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.java` describes a target "identity-v2" shape (`apiVersion: 2`, with `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId` nested under an `identity` object and removed from top level). The current code does NOT implement this — the current DTO exposes those three fields flat at top level and has no `apiVersion`. See section 8.

---

## 1. Owner identity derivation source files

### Region code derivation
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/PostcodeRegion.java` — primary postcode→region lookup. Fixed disjoint ranges: `NSW 2000-2099`, `VIC 3000-3099`, `QLD 4000-4099`. `regionFor(postcode)` parses the trimmed postcode as int and returns the containing region, or `null` if absent/non-numeric/out of range.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/CityRegion.java` — fallback city→region lookup: `Sydney→NSW`, `Melbourne→VIC`, `Brisbane→QLD`, else `"UNKNOWN"`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Locality.java` — combines the two. Postcode takes precedence; only when postcode yields `null` does it fall back to the city table:
```java
public static String of(String city, String postcode) {
    String region = PostcodeRegion.regionFor(postcode);
    return region != null ? region : CityRegion.regionFor(city);
}
```
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/RegionTimezone.java` — region→IANA timezone (`NSW→Australia/Sydney`, `VIC→Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD→Australia/Brisbane`, else `null`).

Note the region is derived once, at member-id minting time, and thereafter read back OUT of the member id (see `Owner.getLocality()` below) rather than recomputed.

### householdId
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/HouseholdIdGenerator.java` — the algorithm:
```java
private static final int LENGTH = 12;
public static String generate(String lastName, String postcode) {
    if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) {
        return null;
    }
    String key = TextNormalizer.normalizeForComparison(lastName) + '|' + postcode;
    return Sha256.hexPrefix(key, LENGTH);
}
```
So householdId = first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 of `normalize(lastName) + "|" + postcode`; `null` when no postcode. Deterministic, so same lastName+postcode share it.

Caveat: the javadoc and the OpenAPI description disagree with the code and each other. The `HouseholdIdGenerator` javadoc says "share a last name and postcode"; the OpenAPI `householdId` description says it is assigned only when `sharesHousehold=true` and keyed on "last name and address". The actual controller (section 7) sets it unconditionally from lastName+postcode regardless of `sharesHousehold`.

### identityKey
Derived inline in `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (see section 2). It is the full 64-char lower-case SHA-256 hex of `telephone + "|" + lowerCased(email or "") + "|" + Soundex(lastName)`.
Supporting utils:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Sha256.java` — `hex()` (full 64-char lower-case) and `hexPrefix(input,length)` (upper-case prefix).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Soundex.java` — 4-char American Soundex.

### memberId
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MemberId.java` — owns the format `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and reads segments back. Build method:
```java
public static String of(String region, int fiscalYearSegment, String normalizedTelephone, String lastName) {
    String base = region
        + String.format("%0" + FISCAL_YEAR_LENGTH + "d", fiscalYearSegment)   // 2-digit FY
        + Sha256.hexPrefix(normalizedTelephone + lastName, HASH_LENGTH);       // HASH8 = 8 upper hex
    return base + Luhn.checkDigit(base);                                       // 1 Luhn check digit
}
```
Read-back: `regionOf(memberId)` = everything before the fixed 11-char trailing part (`FY`=2 + `HASH8`=8 + `CHK`=1 = `TRAILING_LENGTH` 11), ignoring any `-<n>` de-dup suffix. `fiscalYearSegmentOf(memberId)` = the two digits right after the region.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/MemberIdGenerator.java` (`@Component`) — orchestrates and de-duplicates:
```java
public String generate(Owner owner) {
    String region = Locality.of(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode());
    int fiscalYearSegment = FiscalYear.yearSegment(RegistrationDatePolicy.effectiveDate(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    String memberId = MemberId.of(region, fiscalYearSegment, owner.getTelephone(), owner.getLastName());
    return deduplicate(memberId);   // appends "-2", "-3", ... on collision via ownerRepository.existsByMemberId
}
```
Supporting utils:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Luhn.java` — `checkDigit(value)` over the digits only.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/FiscalYear.java` — FY starts 1 July, numbered by the year it ends; `yearSegment` = FY % 100; `label` = `"FY%02d"`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/RegistrationDatePolicy.java` — `effectiveDate()` defaults null→today and rolls weekends/holidays forward; feeds the FY segment.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/TextNormalizer.java` — trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case (used by householdId and namesake counting; NOT by identityKey/memberId telephone).

---

## 2. Owner response DTO / shape

The response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from the `Owner` schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines 2121-2379). It is `OwnerFields` (lines 2001-2120) plus these read-only derived fields. Field list:

From `OwnerFields` (also request-writable): `title` (enum MR/MRS/MS/DR), `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `city`, `postcode`, `telephone`, `email`, `birthDate`, `registrationDate`, `sharesHousehold` (bool, not persisted).

Added read-only in `Owner`: `id`, `selfLink` (`/api/owners/{id}`), `displayName` (`"Last, First"`), `salutation`, `telephoneDisplay`, `memberId`, `fiscalYear` (`FY27`), `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel` (1-4), `householdId`, `identityKey`, `initials`, **`locality`** (e.g. `NSW`), **`timezone`** (e.g. `Australia/Sydney`), `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `riskFlag`, `contactPreference` (EMAIL/PHONE), `ownerSegment` (enum PREMIUM_METRO / PREMIUM_REGIONAL / STANDARD_METRO / STANDARD_REGIONAL), `ageBand` (MINOR/ADULT/SENIOR), `deleted`, `pets` (required).

There is NO `apiVersion` field in the current schema (grep for `apiVersion` hits only the test). `locality` and `timezone` are both present.

The actual field getters live in the entity `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`. Key derived getters:
```java
public String getLocality() {              // read back from member id, not recomputed
    return MemberId.regionOf(this.memberId);
}
public String getTimezone() {
    return RegionTimezone.zoneFor(getLocality());
}
public String getFiscalYear() {
    Integer yearSegment = MemberId.fiscalYearSegmentOf(this.memberId);
    return yearSegment == null ? null : FiscalYear.label(yearSegment);
}
public String getPrimaryIdentifier() { return getMemberId(); }   // used by audit event
public String getIdentityKey() {
    String key = String.join("|",
        this.telephone == null ? "" : this.telephone,
        this.email == null ? "" : this.email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT),
        Soundex.encode(getLastName()));
    return Sha256.hex(key);
}
public String getOwnerSegment() {
    return OwnerSegment.of(getMembershipLevel(), getLocality());
}
```
The mapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct) maps entity→`OwnerDto` and computes `selfLink`, `displayName`, `telephoneDisplay`; also builds `OwnerPageDto` for V2.

---

## 3. Audit event class and schema version handling

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerAuditor.java` (`@Component`) — logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"`. Emits two lines on create: a human-readable line and a JSON serialization (using `tools.jackson` `JsonMapper`) of an `OwnerCreatedEvent`. Holds an `AtomicLong sequence`.
```java
public void ownerCreated(Owner owner) {
    AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} memberId={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel());
    OwnerCreatedEvent event = new OwnerCreatedEvent(this.sequence.incrementAndGet(), owner);
    AUDIT.info(MAPPER.writeValueAsString(event));
}
```
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerCreatedEvent.java` — an immutable `record`:
```java
public record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String memberId, Integer membershipLevel,
                                String event) {
    public static final String OWNER_CREATED = "OWNER_CREATED";
    public OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Owner owner) {
        this(seq, owner.getId(), owner.getPrimaryIdentifier(), owner.getMembershipLevel(), OWNER_CREATED);
    }
}
```
Schema-version handling: there is NO explicit numeric schema-version field on the event today. The only versioning is the `event` discriminator string (`"OWNER_CREATED"`) and the `seq` monotonic counter. The identifier is taken from `getPrimaryIdentifier()` (currently the member id) so it "follows" whatever the primary identifier is. If the task involves adding an audit schema version, this record and `OwnerAuditor` are where it would go. The test-side capture harness is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` logger).

---

## 4. Owner segment derivation logic

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerSegment.java`:
```java
private static final int PREMIUM_MIN_LEVEL = 3;
private static final Set<String> METRO_REGIONS = Set.of("NSW", "VIC", "QLD");
public static String of(Integer membershipLevel, String locality) {
    return tier(membershipLevel) + "_" + area(locality);
}
private static String tier(Integer membershipLevel) {
    return membershipLevel != null && membershipLevel >= PREMIUM_MIN_LEVEL ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
}
private static String area(String locality) {
    return METRO_REGIONS.contains(locality) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
}
```
Called from `Owner.getOwnerSegment()` with `getMembershipLevel()` and `getLocality()`. TIER=PREMIUM at membership level ≥3; AREA=METRO when locality ∈ {NSW,VIC,QLD}.

Related derivation (membership level feeding the tier) is all in `Owner.java`: `getMembershipPoints()` (email +2, no-namesakes +1, household≥3 +2, tenure≥1 FY +3), `getMembershipLevel()` (points→1-4, capped by `membershipLevelCap`).

---

## 5. Request DTOs for the owner endpoint

- `OwnerFields` schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines 2001-2120) → generates `OwnerFieldsDto` (the create/update request body). Fields: `title`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `city`, `postcode`, `telephone`, `email`, `birthDate`, `registrationDate`, `sharesHousehold`. Required: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`. Validation constraints (patterns, lengths) are in the schema; postcode pattern `^[0-9]{4}$`.
- `Idempotency-Key` is a request header, not a DTO field (handled by `IdempotencyKeyStore`).
- Server-side request validation helpers: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/OwnerFieldsValidator.java` (`findMissingFields`), plus normalizers/validators in the same package (`AddressNormalizer`, `EmailNormalizer`, `TelephoneNormalizer`, `PostcodeValidator`, `DisposableEmailValidator`, etc.).

---

## 6. Existing tests related to these

Only three test files exist (no `src/test` unit tests for the util/model classes):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the ONLY functional test; asserts the target identity-v2 shape (see section 8). This test currently would FAIL against the current flat DTO.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base harness. Contains reference tables mirroring the algorithms: `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `HOLIDAYS`, plus `sha256hex`, `shaHex(s,n)`, `luhn(s)`, `toBusinessDay`, and payload builders (`ownerNode`, `structuredOwner`, `knownOwner`, `withPostcode`). Uses `POST /api/owners` + `GET /api/owners/{id}`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — Logback appender helper for asserting `AUDIT` logger output.

---

## 7. Controller and service classes for the owner endpoint

### Controllers
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (implements generated `OwnersApi`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`). Handles `listOwners`, `getOwner`, `addOwner`, `updateOwner`, `deleteOwner`, and pet/visit sub-resources. The `addOwner` flow is where identity derivation is triggered: idempotency check → `resolveAddress` → missing-fields validation → `toOwner` → postcode/city-capacity/future-date/daily-limit checks → telephone+email normalization → disposable-email check → `setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode))` → `setDeclaredHouseholdMember(sharesHousehold)` → `isIdentityDuplicate` check → `saveOwner` (mints memberId etc.) → `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated` → `welcomeNotifier.welcome` → remember idempotency key → DTO with warning flags. It also stamps `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag` on the response via `toOwnerDtoWithWarnings`. Constants: `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY=50`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY=100`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD=80`, `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD=40`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` (implements `OwnerV2Api`) — only a paged `listOwnersPage` returning `OwnerPageDto`.

### Service
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (interface) and `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (impl). `saveOwner` is where identity/derived persistent fields are set on a new owner:
```java
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        if (owner.getMemberId() == null) {
            owner.setMemberId(memberIdGenerator.generate(owner));
        }
        owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCounter.count(owner));
        owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMemberCounter.count(owner));
        owner.setMembershipLevelCap(householdMembershipLevelCeiling.ceilingFor(owner));
        Owner possibleDuplicate = owner.isDeclaredHouseholdMember()
            ? null : possibleDuplicateDetector.findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicate != null);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(possibleDuplicate == null ? null : possibleDuplicate.getId());
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
public boolean isIdentityDuplicate(Owner owner) {
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    return ownerRepository.findByTelephone(owner.getTelephone()).stream()
        .filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())
        .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey()));
}
```

### Supporting `@Component` collaborators (all in `service/`)
- `MemberIdGenerator.java` — memberId (section 1).
- `NamesakeCounter.java` — counts existing owners with same normalized first+last name.
- `HouseholdMembers.java` — returns existing owners sharing this owner's `householdId` (matched among same last name).
- `HouseholdMemberCounter.java` — `householdMembers.of(owner).size() + 1`.
- `HouseholdMembershipLevelCeiling.java` — `max(existing household member level) + 1`, else null.
- `PossibleDuplicateDetector.java` — same postcode + same Soundex(lastName) + DIFFERENT identityKey, earliest by id, ignoring soft-deleted.
- `OwnerAuditor.java` / `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` — audit (section 3).
- `WelcomeNotifier.java`, `IdempotencyKeyStore.java` — side effects.

Entity + persistence: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (columns `member_id`, `household_id`, `namesake_count`, `household_size`, `membership_level_cap`, `possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`, `deleted`; `@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()` applies `RegistrationDatePolicy`). Repository `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` (`existsByMemberId`, `findByTelephone`, `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`, `countByCity`, etc.).

---

## 8. Key finding: current vs. target "identity-v2" shape

`AcceptanceTest.java` encodes a not-yet-implemented contract:
```
apiVersion == 2
$.identity.memberId / $.identity.identityKey / $.identity.householdId  -> present
$.memberId / $.identityKey / $.householdId (top level)                 -> must NOT exist
```
Current reality:
- `openapi.yml` Owner schema has `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` FLAT at top level and no `apiVersion` and no nested `identity` object.
- To satisfy the test you would need to: add `apiVersion` (constant 2) and a nested `identity` object schema to the `Owner` schema, move the three fields into it, and update `OwnerMapper` (and/or a wrapper) to populate the nested object. No code path currently produces `apiVersion` or a nested `identity`.

All derivation algorithms (region, householdId, identityKey, memberId, audit) are quoted above and would carry over unchanged into a nested representation — only the response shape/wiring differs.

