## 3. Audit event class and schema version handling

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerAuditor.java` (`@Component`) — logs to a dedicated SLF4J logger named `"AUDIT"`. Emits two lines on create: a human-readable line and a JSON serialization (using `tools.jackson` `JsonMapper`) of an `OwnerCreatedEvent`. Holds an `AtomicLong sequence`.
```java
public void ownerCreated(Owner owner) {
    AUDIT.info("Owner created: id={} memberId={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel());
    OwnerCreatedEvent event = new OwnerCreatedEvent(this.sequence.incrementAndGet(), owner);
    AUDIT.info(MAPPER.writeValueAsString(event));
}
```
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/OwnerCreatedEvent.java` — an immutable `record`:
```java
public record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String memberId, Integer membershipLevel,
                                String event) {
    public static final String OWNER_CREATED = "OWNER_CREATED";
    public OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Owner owner) {
        this(seq, owner.getId(), owner.getPrimaryIdentifier(), owner.getMembershipLevel(), OWNER_CREATED);
    }
}
```
Schema-version handling: there is NO explicit numeric schema-version field on the event today. The only versioning is the `event` discriminator string (`"OWNER_CREATED"`) and the `seq` monotonic counter. The identifier is taken from `getPrimaryIdentifier()` (currently the member id) so it "follows" whatever the primary identifier is. If the task involves adding an audit schema version, this record and `OwnerAuditor` are where it would go. The test-side capture harness is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (attaches a Logback `ListAppender` to the `AUDIT` logger).

