## 7. Controller and service classes for the owner endpoint

### Controllers
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (implements generated `OwnersApi`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`). Handles `listOwners`, `getOwner`, `addOwner`, `updateOwner`, `deleteOwner`, and pet/visit sub-resources. The `addOwner` flow is where identity derivation is triggered: idempotency check → `resolveAddress` → missing-fields validation → `toOwner` → postcode/city-capacity/future-date/daily-limit checks → telephone+email normalization → disposable-email check → `setHouseholdId(HouseholdIdGenerator.generate(lastName, postcode))` → `setDeclaredHouseholdMember(sharesHousehold)` → `isIdentityDuplicate` check → `saveOwner` (mints memberId etc.) → `ownerAuditor.ownerCreated` → `welcomeNotifier.welcome` → remember idempotency key → DTO with warning flags. It also stamps `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag` on the response via `toOwnerDtoWithWarnings`. Constants: `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY=50`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY=100`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD=80`, `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD=40`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` (implements `OwnerV2Api`) — only a paged `listOwnersPage` returning `OwnerPageDto`.

### Service
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (interface) and `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (impl). `saveOwner` is where identity/derived persistent fields are set on a new owner:
```java
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) {
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        if (owner.getMemberId() == null) {
            owner.setMemberId(memberIdGenerator.generate(owner));
        }
        owner.setNamesakeCount(namesakeCounter.count(owner));
        owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMemberCounter.count(owner));
        owner.setMembershipLevelCap(householdMembershipLevelCeiling.ceilingFor(owner));
        Owner possibleDuplicate = owner.isDeclaredHouseholdMember()
            ? null : possibleDuplicateDetector.findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(possibleDuplicate != null);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(possibleDuplicate == null ? null : possibleDuplicate.getId());
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
public boolean isIdentityDuplicate(Owner owner) {
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    return ownerRepository.findByTelephone(owner.getTelephone()).stream()
        .filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())
        .anyMatch(existing -> identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey()));
}
```

### Supporting `@Component` collaborators (all in `service/`)
- `MemberIdGenerator.java` — memberId (section 1).
- `NamesakeCounter.java` — counts existing owners with same normalized first+last name.
- `HouseholdMembers.java` — returns existing owners sharing this owner's `householdId` (matched among same last name).
- `HouseholdMemberCounter.java` — `householdMembers.of(owner).size() + 1`.
- `HouseholdMembershipLevelCeiling.java` — `max(existing household member level) + 1`, else null.
- `PossibleDuplicateDetector.java` — same postcode + same Soundex(lastName) + DIFFERENT identityKey, earliest by id, ignoring soft-deleted.
- `OwnerAuditor.java` / `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` — audit (section 3).
- `WelcomeNotifier.java`, `IdempotencyKeyStore.java` — side effects.

Entity + persistence: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` (columns `member_id`, `household_id`, `namesake_count`, `household_size`, `membership_level_cap`, `possible_duplicate`, `possible_duplicate_of`, `deleted`; `@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate()` applies `RegistrationDatePolicy`). Repository `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` (`existsByMemberId`, `findByTelephone`, `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`, `countByCity`, etc.).

